---@meta
-- Generated by rs3-api-types from https://developer.runescape.com/rs/core/clientoptions.html;
-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---Client options represent configurable game client settings, ranging from graphical settings such as draw distance and
---ground decor, to audio volume levels, and accessibility options like cutscene subtitles and cursor scales.
---
---Info: These represent the options available at the game client/engine-level, independent of actual game content,
---hence they do not include the various options listed in the ingame gameplay settings interface for example.
---
---The various options are contained within the `game.options` table, with the following options being available:
---@class ClientOption
---@field hasLabels boolean (Read-only) True if there are text labels for this option's values, false otherwise.
---@field isToggle boolean (Read-only) True if this a on/off toggle setting instead of supporting arbitrary values.
---@field isModifiable boolean (Read-only) True if this option can be currently modified. Some settings may not be modified in certain cases where there's a dependency on other settings. For example, you can't change the shadow quality level if shadows are disabled.
---@field setting integer The current setting for this option.
---@field min integer (Read-only) The minimum setting this option can be set to.
---@field max integer (Read-only) The maximum setting this option can be set to.
---@field minMaxRange integer (Read-only) Returns the minimum and maximum values this option can be set to. In the client: It reads one number, 0 for Brightness, not a pair.
local ClientOption = {}

---Sets this option to the specified setting.
---@param setting integer The setting to set this option to.
---@return boolean # True if this option was successfully changed to the provided setting, false otherwise.
function ClientOption:Set(setting) end

---Checks if the specified setting is valid for this option.
---@param setting integer The setting to check for validity.
---@return boolean # True if this option supports being set to the provided setting, false otherwise.
function ClientOption:CheckIsValidSetting(setting) end

---Gets the user-friendly text label associated with the provided setting for this option.
---
---Warning: This function is non-localised currently, always returning english text.
---@param setting integer The setting to retrieve the text label for.
---@return string? # The text label associated with the provided setting, or nil if the setting is invalid or has no associated text.
function ClientOption:GetLabel(setting) end

